{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3310","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3310","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3310\",\"parent_revision\":\"00e6615b175d84096e6129400b8d962dc2cb6673258103646b145df2672c4228\",\"root_revision\":\"00e6615b175d84096e6129400b8d962dc2cb6673258103646b145df2672c4228\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe need this serves: prevent a crafted search query from hanging the backlog process.\\n\\n**Observed**: `apply_search_filter` (backlog_core/search.py:68) compiles and executes user-supplied regex terms (`/pattern/` or `regex:pattern` syntax) with Python's backtracking `re` engine and no timeout or complexity bound. This pattern predates #3169 (moved unchanged from server.py during the search-engine extraction), but #3169 newly exposes it through the CLI `--search` flag (`sam_schema/backlog.py list_items`) in addition to the existing MCP `backlog_list` tool \u2014 widening the reachable surface for a crafted catastrophic-backtracking pattern (e.g. nested quantifiers like `(a+)+b`) to cause CPU exhaustion (ReDoS) on the backlog process.\\n\\n**Impact**: any caller of `backlog list --search` or `backlog_list(search=...)` \u2014 including agents constructing queries from user-supplied title/description text (see `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3) \u2014 can trigger pathological regex backtracking.\\n\\n**Fix direction (from review, not prescriptive)**: bound regex evaluation with a timeout (e.g. `regex` module's timeout support, or a `signal.alarm`/thread-based watchdog), or validate/reject patterns with nested quantifiers before compiling.\\n\\n**Source**: Surfaced during the multi-perspective security review of #3169 (content-based duplicate detection), verdict APPROVE with this MINOR finding noted as non-blocking follow-up.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Multi-perspective review follow-up on #3169 (security perspective, review-3169-20260829T020754Z)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"693c2973c9bb52d5b31d7ee58561ab1ec326f2812cd531f2c1dc35f205392bdc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5ZLA\"}"}